    "result_text": "All 280 tests pass, including the new Cp16 test. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented for the `namesakeCount` feature:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema (which regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter, following the same pattern as `membershipNumber`/`customerCode`/`membershipTier`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Before saving, it now sets `namesakeCount` via a new `countNamesakes(lastName)` helper that counts existing owners sharing the same last name (case-insensitively) *at that moment*. Since the new owner isn't persisted yet, this counts only the *other* owners.\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `namesake_count` column so the persisted value survives the follow-up `GET`.\n\nMapStruct maps the field automatically since the names match. The first owner with a surname gets `0`, the second gets `1`, matching the acceptance test.",
